# Canonical author identity — collapses the two commit-name spellings
# ("vadimtoptunov" from the CLI, "Vadim Toptunov" from GitHub-side merge
# commits) into one person, so contributor views (GitHub, Swift Package Index,
# `git shortlog`) show a single author instead of two.
